2026-03-15T00:00:00Z | RALPH R1 | Inter-camp and institutional connections research. 18 web searches conducted. 27 new facts (f_0725-f_0751), 10 new sources (total: 165). Key findings:
  - Camp Weredale: Founded 1934 by Rotary Club of Westmount on Lac l'Achigan. YMCA proposed Kanawana-Weredale two-site operation in 1977 (Concordia Archives 12A).
  - Camp Otoreke: Renamed from Camp Jubilee in 1909, operated until 1982 at Lake St. Joseph, Saint-Adolphe-d'Howard. YMCA camping started there 1892 (Lemuel Cushing).
  - Camp Ouareau: Founded 1922 by Mabel Jamieson (who was YMCA Montreal secretary general) and Ferna Halliday. Girls camp, not YMCA-operated.
  - YWCA Camp Oolahwan: Founded 1917, centennial at Camp Ouareau 2017.
  - Big Cove YMCA Camp (NS, 1889): Oldest in Canada. Kanawana (1894): Oldest in Quebec, second oldest in Canada.
  - Camp Pine Crest (ON, 1910): YMCA of Greater Toronto. John Island Camp (ON, 1954): YMCA of Northeastern Ontario.
  - CCA founded 1936 at Central YMCA Toronto. OCA archives have Kanawana file dated 1940.
  - Stuart McLean: Counsellor at Kanawana 1969-early 1970s, attended Sir George Williams/Concordia. Fund established 2017.
  - 1993 documentary "Kamp Kanawana: The Experience that lasts a lifetime" (Concordia Archives).
  - Concordia Archives Sub-series 12L holds Camp Jubilee records: fishing rights (1893-1902), photos (1898), brochures (1898-1900).
  - No direct connection found for Lower Canada College or McGill Daily to Kanawana. McGill Garage Band Camp visited Kanawana (Facebook).
  - YMCA Quebec discontinued day camps (including Concordia-based ones) fall 2025; Kanawana summer camp continues.
