[2026-08-14] Research agent returns: Montreal YMCA leadership, Camp Pascobac, Rob Braide -- three long-standing questions RESOLVED against primary sources
  - A deep-research agent (53 tool calls, ~16 web queries plus direct fetches and full-text grep of 13 digitized YMCA of Montreal annual reports) settled three questions the p_218 audit had flagged as needing conflict records. In two of the three, NO conflict record was needed after all -- the apparent disagreements dissolved once the primary sources were read.
  - ROSS BANNERMAN -- the "late 1970s" was a MISREADING OF A SINGLE YEAR. An Internet Archive news release dated 1970-11-27 announces his appointment as General Secretary and CEO of the Montreal YMCA effective DECEMBER 1, 1970, succeeding Rix G. Rogers, aged 43 (implying b. c.1927). The Camp Stephens alumni blog's "became CEO in the late 1970s" -- which this wiki repeated -- turned "late 1970" into "the late 1970s". Annual-report mastheads 1970-71 through 1977-78 confirm his continuous tenure; the 1978-79 report shows Kerry W. Johnston in the office and narrates the handover. So by the late 1970s his tenure was ENDING, not beginning.
  - RICHARD PATTEN -- branch, not association, and the wiki's inference was FALSE. The 1977-78 and 1978-79 annual reports list him under "Branch Chairmen and Executive Directors" as head of the Centre-ville/Downtown BRANCH, in a different section from the Metropolitan Staff masthead naming the association's General Secretary. Camping and Outdoor Education was its own parallel branch (D. Walsh, then D. Twynam). Patten therefore held NO line authority over Kanawana. The Canadian Parliamentary Guide's compressed "Exec. Dir., YMCA, Montreal, 1976-79" -- inherited by his Wikipedia entry and obituary -- simply omits the branch.
  - NOTABLE PROCESS POINT: p_222 had "fixed" the Patten sentence in between-centennials.md three hours earlier by giving it a citation. The citation was fine; the CLAIM was false. VERIFY (does every claim carry a marker, and does the marker point at the right source?) is not the same as RESEARCH (is the claim true?). A clean VERIFY pass cannot catch a well-cited falsehood. Recorded here because it bears on how much assurance the p_218 sweep's "clean" verdicts actually carry.
  - CAMP PASCOBAC -- confirmed at Kars, New Brunswick, on Belleisle Bay, Kings County, operated for 50 years by the Y's Men's Club of Saint John together with the YMCA from a May 1928 land purchase until its sale to the Province of New Brunswick. NOT Manitoba. This closes the p_225 blocking finding directly: ross-bannerman.md said "Camp Pascobac and Camp Stephens in Manitoba", attaching Manitoba to both when it belongs only to Stephens. The New Brunswick location also fits the recruitment chronology -- McEwen recruited Bannerman at the SAINT JOHN YMCA.
  - ROB BRAIDE -- broadcasting-history.ca's CJAD station history states plainly that in 1987 "Rob Braide became vice president and general manager of CJAD/CJFM-FM." He was NEVER President of Standard Broadcasting Corporation: Allan Slaight owned and led it, and Gary Slaight was president of Standard Radio from 1987 -- the man who hired Braide. The likely origin of the error is his later role as President of BRAIDE MEDIA appearing in the same short biography. directors-index.md (E1-reviewed) corrected; rob-braide.md upgraded from "General Manager" to "Vice President and General Manager"; the outstanding VERIFY item (b) on that article closed WITHOUT a conflict record, since there was no genuine two-source disagreement -- one source was simply wrong.
  - NEW FINDING, narrowing a documented gap: Kamp Kanawana director's and annual reports ARE digitized and full-text searchable on Internet Archive (rma-concordia-publications) -- 1964-1966, 1969-1971, 1974-1979, 1987, plus Ka-News 1977-1981. The 1976 and 1977 director's reports are signed "Derek V. Walsh, Director of Camping" and the 1979 report "G. David Twynam / Director". between-centennials.md had stated "No director is confirmed for 1976-1978"; Walsh is now documented in camping leadership for two of those three years, leaving only 1978 unaccounted. Caveat preserved in-article: "Director of Camping" is the BRANCH title and does not by itself establish on-site camp direction.
  - This also CORRECTS ross-bannerman.md Open Question 2, which asserted "Physical archive consultation is the only path" to the 1970-1975 director's reports. It is not -- several are digitized. Reading them is now a desk task.
  - kb/facts.json: +7 (f_2020-f_2026), now 1988, v5.16 -> v5.17. sources/sources.json: +5 primary/secondary records, now 657. Verified: 736 cross-links, 0 broken; harness A2 issues cleared.

