2026-09-03 Read the 1965 Kanawana annual report in full. Nine new facts. Co-ed camping PROPOSED for the 1966 season in the report itself, with a costed design (Woodsmen section, eight units four and four, a partition in the toilet building, $300-400 for a girls' wash house) -- two years before the 1967-1970 pilot this wiki dates it to -- plus the earlier Keith Farquharson constituency survey and the Metropolitan Board's deferral. coeducation-gender.md restructured accordingly. First T-Group laboratory staff training, trainers Ted Lowe, Bruce McFarlane, Ray Rouse and Rix Rogers. The Kanawana-Tamaracouta Trail opened in week 7, following the 1964 joint land purchase. The camp bell cracked when struck with a hatchet while tolling for a lost camper. Mrs Tasse documented as camp staff (laundry, feeding the advance party six weeks before opening); Julien cut 22,000 board feet and 100 cords over the winter. Worst registration in years: 1,200 camper weeks against 1,500, with six stated causes including "Kanawana is not seen as a status camp". SELF-CORRECTION: f_2401 first claimed the 1950s Rangers section was new; section-names.md already had it from other reports. Corrected in place. KB 5.87 -> 5.88.
2026-09-03 Read the 1966, 1969 and 1970 Kanawana reports in full. 1966: almost pure statistics, two facts previously taken from it, everything else left -- pre-season hours and costs, season consumption, a payroll working out to 27.1 cents/hour, a ten-year summary with religion and age breakdowns and a camper geography by Montreal district, and the camp's own claim of 73 years of CONTINUOUS operation from 1894. 1969: CIT programme went co-ed and dropped table-waiting the same year (12 male, 4 female, model camp built on Lake Wilson); 125 weeks of camperships; horseback riding and stables two years before the finding aid dates them; Anderson arguing for year-round use of the property. 1970: first Cystic Fibrosis campers (7); the fullest early-coeducation account held here; Becsies and Page's shown to be AREAS OF the Kanawana property with transient young people camping there; 14 renting groups named; kitchen catered out for the first time; Julien Tasse named again. KB 5.88 -> 5.91.
