2026-09-03 Built kb/restricted/ at operator request: a register of WITHHELD material that holds none of it. Forced by the finding that github.com/mattaronson/Kanawana is PUBLIC -- there is no confidential file in this repo, so the register is content-free by design and records only existence, locator, category, reason, embargo and review date. scripts/verify/restricted_guard.py enforces both halves: no content fields in the register, and no restricted name in kb/facts.json or wiki/, deriving the names from the source at runtime and storing nothing. Regression-tested by planting one restricted name in facts.json (guard failed, exit 1, printed no names) and removing it (guard passed). First entry r_0001: the 1973 director's report Recommendations section, 5 subjects, review 2055 (later of record+75 and birth+100). CLAUDE.md Phase 2 privacy rule amended from "do not extract" to "withhold, register, and publish what survives the removal" -- the old rule lost material silently. Queued p_306 (operator decision on the public raw corpus in sources/cache/, which predates this register and sits in git history) and p_307 (retrospective sweep for withholdings made before the register existed). Verified kb/facts.json and wiki/ are clean of the r_0001 names. KB 6.01 -> 6.02.
2026-09-03 Rebuilt the restricted design around the operator's boundary: the archive is public and the OCR corpus in the repo is fine; the questionable act is pushing named personal material into the PUBLISHED WIKI. So restricted material is now EXTRACTED into kb/facts.json with a publication block (status/register_id/review_on/basis/why) rather than kept out of the KB, and gated at wiki/. f_2466 and f_2467 written (the 1973 staff recommendations; the 1975 identification-by-inference risk). Register rewritten to point at fact ids. restricted_guard.py rewritten as a publication gate. TWO BUGS IN THE GATE, BOTH FAILING OPEN, both caught by its own regression test rather than by reading it: the name extractor matched only title case so names written in capitals passed through, and a debugging session had put two of the protected surnames in the stopword list. Fixed: case-tolerant matching, case-insensitive comparison, corpus-derived common-word filter keeping a pair when EITHER token is uncommon (requiring both dropped "Pierre Parizeau", since "pierre" is an ordinary French word), and a STOP list restricted to role and place words with a comment forbidding surnames. Regression: planting all five restricted names in an article flags four -- the fifth is Paul Mongraw, legitimately in the wiki for directing Les Voyageurs, correctly excluded. p_306 resolved by operator decision. p_308 queued: wire the gate into build-content.ts before publication. KB 6.02 -> 6.03.
2026-09-03 Third and final shape for the sensitive-material design, set by the operator: the record comes first, embargo is METADATA not deletion, and publication policy belongs to the wiki UI layer rather than to collection. Nothing is now withheld from kb/facts.json or wiki/ -- both are kept complete. The 1973 staff recommendations are written into people/leo-robitaille.md inside an <!-- embargo:r_0001 --> block with context supplied outside it. restricted_guard.py rewritten a third time: it now checks LABELLING (every embargoed fact registered and dated, every marker paired and resolving, no embargoed-only name appearing outside a block) rather than blocking anything. A THIRD fail-open bug was found by regression: the check asked whether a name appeared INSIDE some block, so a name both properly blocked and loose in the prose passed; fixed by stripping blocks and searching the remainder. All three of this script's bugs were caught by planting a name and watching, never by reading it. p_308 reframed from a build hook to a UI design decision. KB 6.03 -> 6.04.
2026-09-04 Added .github/workflows/verify.yml: the four verification scripts now run on every push and PR. Two blockers had to be fixed first. verify_harness.py had NO sys.exit -- it reported everything and always exited 0, so nothing it found could fail a build; it now exits 1 on blocking classes (A1/A2/B/D/E/F/G plus the three whole-wiki passes) and 0 on advisory (check C, provenance H-M). And three scripts hardcoded ROOT='/home/user/Kanawana', which exists only in the session container; verify_harness.py now derives it from __file__. New scripts/verify/data_integrity.py: JSON/JSONL parse, id uniqueness and format, fact_count agreement, publication.status vocabulary, and a regeneration check that rebuilds person-index.json and the multi-year table into a scratch copy and fails if the committed files differ. The 20 duplicate source_ids are reported ADVISORY, not blocking -- pre-existing and queued as p_303; a check earns the right to fail a build by being actionable by whoever just pushed. Both new exit paths tested by planting defects (an unresolvable marker in a body; a header miscounting its own list). Validated by cloning the repo to /tmp and running all four from a different path: all green.
