2026-09-05T00:00:00Z  RESEARCH  p_408 closed, and its premise was wrong. Know History's "Rooted: Beausoleil Island" is not a commissioned written study with chapters; it is an EIGHT-CHAPTER AUDIO PODCAST published 18 October 2021, hosted by Liz Edwards, "an auditory experience... using soundscapes, storytelling, interviews, and historic texts." There was never anything to read. The HTTP 403 this project recorded was a true fact about the fetch tool and a misleading one about the object: a plain request with a browser user-agent gets 404 on the chapter path and 200 on the site, which is how the medium came out. Chapter 5, 12 minutes 10 seconds, has now been heard: no transcript is published, so the audio was downloaded and transcribed in-session with faster-whisper (small, int8) and the text cached at sources/cache/podcasts/ under a header saying exactly what it is and how it was made. CONTENT: the archaeology of the camp's sandy point (artefacts to about 5,000 years, some archaic material older), the camp's partnership with Parks Canada, and former camper and director Brian Shelley on what the place did for him. EXPLICIT NULL ON THE L&V GAMES: lumberman, voyageur, games, competition, team, colour war, Kanawana and Pine Crest do not occur in the 1,412-word transcript in any spelling variant searched (f_4841). The caveat travels with the null -- a machine transcript is evidence about the audio filtered through a model, never checked by ear, and the model mangles every proper noun in the file. ALSO: the chapter states 1919 twice, "In 2019, Camp Kitchikewana celebrated its 100th anniversary" and "Since 1919, campers have gathered together on Kitchikewana sands" -- a third voice for 1919 against the 1921 of Blackstock's obituary and the Ebbs tribute, but not an independent one, since the camp took part in the programme; f_4768's conflict stands (f_4842). CHANGED: src_knowhistory_beausoleil corrected as to medium, URL and read_state; src_rooted_beausoleil_ch5 added; f_476