2026-09-05T00:00:00Z  VERIFY  p_403 CLOSED after a second pass the same day, from artefacts rather than reports. The annual reports run out long before the record does, and two bodies of physical evidence already held here carry the seasons they skip. THE PLAQUE CORPUS: the person index built from the boards (p_291) carries dated appearances for 1955, 1956, 1959-65, 1968, 1970, 1972, 1973, 1975, 1979-90 and 1992-2010. A board naming a cabin's campers and their counsellor was made at camp, in that summer, for those people -- direct physical evidence the season ran. That closes 1981-84, 1989-90, 1992-93, 1995-97, 2002-04 and 2006-2010 (f_4850). It gives no attendance: the corpus counts whoever appears on boards that survived, two names in 1987 against 205 in 2008. THE L&V TROPHY: a shield for every season 1947-2025 except 2021, transcribed in full, which closes every remaining year from 1976 forward -- AND CARRIES ITS OWN WARNING. There is a 2020 shield and the camp did not run in 2020; the Games were played remotely by alumni and campers from their homes. So a shield attests a season and not necessarily a RESIDENTIAL one, and that is the single year in seventy-nine where the two come apart, documented as such (f_4851, f_2007). Recorded rather than smoothed over, because it is exactly what a later reader would otherwise have to rediscover. 1906 ALSO CLOSED, from the report for the year ending 30 April 1907: the season in its own words, Victoria Day party 24 May, Business Boys 16-30 June, School Boys 30 June-14 July, Senior Camp 14 July-8 September, and an attendance table totalling 216 -- only the total legible in the OCR, the four components sitting on the printed page for whoever reaches it (f_4852). STILL BLANK: 1911, 1914 and 1920, three seasons, each needing one specific volume (the annual reports published 1912, 1915 and 1921), none in the digitized run. Queued as p_420 with four routes named. CHANGED: attendance-series.md gains a second fill section and a 1906 