tches exact strings, and 'Anne I. Vail' now scores 0 articles while the same woman appears across the wiki as NAN VAIL and ANN VAIL, including in the Shorgan article written hours ago. Both lists are approximations and any pass acting on them must search the variants first. All six verify scripts pass.
2026-09-05T00:00:00Z  WRITE  p_402 closed, as instructed: FOLDED IN, NO STUBS SPAWNED. canadian-camping-movement.md gains "The people this article's sources keep naming", covering all nine individuals who held substantial fact records and appeared in no wiki article: Wallace Forgie (1883-1967), the "Commodore" of 1908-1927 in Canada and Adele Ebbs's uncle, who took her on her first big canoe trip at ten -- which is where the movement's matriarch learned to trip; Elsie K. and David Palter of Camp Kawagama, on the editorial team of The Camp Counselor's Book, with Elsie Palter's 1964 use of Maslow (probably its earliest appearance in Canadian camping literature) and her 1970 taxonomy of why children steal at camp; John Hoyle, chair of the standards committee 1947-1950 and author of the frankest ethics gloss in the run ("bidding up on honoraria"); Keith Cleverdon, who wrote that committee's documentary history in 1955; M. C. MacCulloch of Bolton Camp, whose 1969 discipline policy says "In no instance may justice at camp take the form of physical punishment. We are not parents and these are not our children"; Elizabeth Wardley Raymer, whose 1958 account of a fouled canoe-trip site argues leave-no-trace twenty years early; Doug Dent of the 1974 Task Force; and Sam Hambly, whose composting pamphlet opened the association's bilingual HOW TO series. The section states why they are folded rather than spawned: none is documented as having any contact with Kanawana, and their claim is on THIS article as the people whose written work the movement ran on. THE COVERAGE CHECK FAILED TWICE WHILE BEING USED, and both failures are now recorded in the article. (1) NAME VARIANTS: it scored "Anne I. Vail" at zero while the same woman is across this wiki as Nan Vail and Ann Vail. (2) LINE WRAPPING: a re-check immediately after writing reported "Elsie Palter" still absent, because the new paragraph had wrapped between her given name and her surname so the string never occurred contiguously